              Purpose
              Using parallel transmission (pTx) in ultra‐high field MRI allows efficient radiofrequency pulse designs that can produce uniform excitations. Here, we demonstrate that pTx can simultaneously mitigate  non‐uniformity and off‐resonance artifacts in balanced steady‐state free precession sequences at 7 T.
            
            
